1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,521
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:29,612
<i>Thank you, Jaguar, but I need</i>
<i>to go back to the mansion</i>

6
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,906
<i>to find out the truth about my mother.</i>

7
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:35,076
[Ivy] <i>The one who helped Emilia escape</i>

8
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:38,663
<i>was none other than Jaguar.</i>

9
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:41,583
-<i>The Ardientes' men!</i>
-[gunshot]

10
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:44,085
[Julio] <i>Jaguar helped you escape.</i>

11
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:48,506
<i>You have been working with him all along!</i>

12
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:51,050
<i>-Get out of my house!</i>
<i>-Papa.</i>

13
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:54,345
[Julio] <i>And never set foot</i>
<i>in this house again!</i>

14
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:57,766
[Camia] <i>Diego, this is the day</i>
<i>we've been waiting for.</i>

15
00:00:57,849 --> 00:01:00,226
<i>I will be the governor of this town.</i>

16
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,312
<i>For a new Ardiente!</i>

17
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,022
[Diego] <i>I have a plan.</i>

18
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:07,692
<i>And in this plan,</i>
<i>my victory will be certain.</i>

19
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:10,445
<i>We'll just have to blow things up.</i>

20
00:01:10,528 --> 00:01:12,363
[explosion]

21
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:14,699
[Ivy] <i>Mom, it's Uncle Damian. He escaped.</i>

22
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:16,076
<i>He was never released from jail.</i>

23
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:18,787
[Damian] <i>You, Emilia,</i>
<i>are the one responsible</i>

24
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:21,706
<i>for my brother's death.</i>

25
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:25,460
<i>I'll make sure you pay for what you did.</i>

26
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:26,795
[Diego] <i>Julio, your time is up.</i>

27
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:28,838
<i>I'll make sure that from this day on,</i>

28
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:31,633
<i>evil will no longer reign in Ardiente.</i>

29
00:01:31,716 --> 00:01:33,968
[woman] <i>Diego's in the lead in</i>
<i>most of the neighborhoods.</i>

30
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:37,514
<i>This fight isn't over.</i>
<i>Let's all just celebrate, okay?</i>

31
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:45,396
Batch! Batch! Guys, it's here.

32
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,607
The unofficial tally from city hall.

33
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:50,527
Diego's ahead by 30,000 votes.

34
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,403
[cheering]

35
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:54,197
-[man] Bro.
-Hold on, hold on.

36
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,448
That's not all,

37
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:57,450
because the towns
that haven't been tallied

38
00:01:57,534 --> 00:01:59,077
are the towns of our supporters.

39
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,329
-Wow.
-So, this is a sure win!

40
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:03,957
[cheering]

41
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,708
[Marlon] It's a sure win, Batch.

42
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:10,797
I'm sure, Diego. You've won.
Congratulations!

43
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,882
[cheering]

44
00:02:19,013 --> 00:02:21,141
[reporter] <i>Let's head over</i>
<i>to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

45
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,101
<i>Diego Torillo has a lead</i>

46
00:02:23,184 --> 00:02:26,646
<i>over Congressman Julio Ardiente</i>
<i>in the votes.</i>

47
00:02:26,729 --> 00:02:27,689
Wow.

48
00:02:27,772 --> 00:02:31,734
It looks like the bastard,
Diego, is going to win.

49
00:02:31,818 --> 00:02:34,445
Boo, Papa! You deserve that.

50
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:37,699
For once, you'll know
the feeling of being a loser.

51
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:48,126
[ominous music playing]

52
00:02:58,011 --> 00:03:00,221
-This is our victory.
-[phone rings]

53
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:02,181
[indistinct chatter]

54
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:03,808
Excuse me, Auntie.

55
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,101
[Loring] Are you okay?

56
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:09,731
[phone ringing]

57
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:15,987
Diego.

58
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:19,407
-Julio.
-[chuckles]

59
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:25,997
Until now, I'm still not used
to you not calling me Grandpa.

60
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:27,624
What do you want?

61
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:29,292
You want me to tell you straight?

62
00:03:30,668 --> 00:03:33,755
I would like you to concede.

63
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:35,798
Concede?

64
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:38,384
You want <i>me</i> to give up?

65
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:42,096
Around 11 in the evening…

66
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:46,476
you can clear out your things
from the polling precinct.

67
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,269
Afterward…

68
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:52,106
Tell the people that you're conceding

69
00:03:52,190 --> 00:03:54,943
the governorship to your grandpa.

70
00:03:55,818 --> 00:03:57,570
Because the truth is…

71
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,448
you love me,

72
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:03,910
and you have complete faith
in my leadership.

73
00:04:04,869 --> 00:04:06,162
<i>And most of all…</i>

74
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:12,335
it's important to you
that we all get along.

75
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:18,383
Because, at the end of it all,
we're family, aren't we?

76
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,593
I won't do that.

77
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:24,347
It's time for the lives of the people

78
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,849
you've been stepping on to get better.

79
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:30,561
So, Julio, say goodbye to your throne.

80
00:04:48,955 --> 00:04:51,040
[phone rings]

81
00:04:57,588 --> 00:04:58,548
Ivy.

82
00:04:58,631 --> 00:05:01,509
Diego. Did Julio call you?

83
00:05:01,884 --> 00:05:03,553
Yes, Ivy, he did.

84
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:06,597
He wanted me to concede,
but there's nothing he can do

85
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:08,599
because the counting is almost over.

86
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:10,560
[scoffs] Ivy.

87
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:12,145
Ivy, we're going to win.

88
00:05:12,228 --> 00:05:16,566
You're right, but we need to
know what Julio's next plan is.

89
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:18,192
Yes.

90
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:21,904
But, Ivy…

91
00:05:23,781 --> 00:05:25,742
Ivy, I want to thank you.

92
00:05:27,076 --> 00:05:28,578
Congrats, Governor.

93
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:32,040
You're the reason I won this.

94
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:36,461
This is the victory
we've all been fighting for.

95
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:39,505
<i>So, thank you.</i>

96
00:05:40,923 --> 00:05:42,133
Thank you for everything.

97
00:05:43,801 --> 00:05:44,886
I have to go.

98
00:05:57,065 --> 00:06:02,945
[singsongs] Papa is a big loser.
Big, big, loser.

99
00:06:03,738 --> 00:06:04,989
Hi, Miss Beautiful.

100
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:07,992
Don't come near me. Stay there.

101
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:09,660
Don't come any closer.

102
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,996
Stay there! [shrieks]

103
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,956
-Give me your cell phone.
-You can't escape.

104
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,792
[shrieks] Let go of me!

105
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:17,043
[groans]

106
00:06:17,126 --> 00:06:18,169
Don't fight back.

107
00:06:18,252 --> 00:06:20,254
-[smack]
-[groans]

108
00:06:22,131 --> 00:06:23,174
Let's go.

109
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:26,010
[Emilia] Let go of me!

110
00:06:26,094 --> 00:06:27,220
[man 1] Over there.

111
00:06:27,303 --> 00:06:28,679
Here.

112
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:31,349
Get your hands off me.

113
00:06:31,432 --> 00:06:32,725
-Let go…
-Over there, dude.

114
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:34,894
[groans]

115
00:06:36,687 --> 00:06:38,940
-You filthy animals!
-[laughing]

116
00:06:39,023 --> 00:06:40,441
Don't come near me!

117
00:06:41,025 --> 00:06:42,610
I'll have you killed.

118
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:45,905
He called you filthy, dude.
Have your way with her!

119
00:06:45,988 --> 00:06:47,907
-This is nice, dude.
-Stay away from me.

120
00:06:47,990 --> 00:06:49,700
I'll finally taste a rich girl.

121
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:51,869
-Hurry up!
-Please! Don't come near me!

122
00:06:51,953 --> 00:06:53,913
Nothing personal, Miss Beautiful.

123
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:56,249
[grunts]

124
00:06:56,332 --> 00:06:57,458
Just relax!

125
00:06:57,542 --> 00:06:59,127
[shrieking]

126
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,503
Just relax, Miss Beautiful.

127
00:07:00,586 --> 00:07:02,255
-Let go of me!
-[laughter]

128
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:04,590
She's like a wild horse!

129
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:06,926
-[groaning]
-[smack]

130
00:07:07,009 --> 00:07:10,054
-Go on.
-I told you to relax.

131
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,139
[Emilia groans]

132
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:13,933
-No. No…
-Why are you so stubborn?

133
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:16,769
Have us killed, huh? Yeah, right!

134
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:20,940
-[laughing]
-No. No. No.

135
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:24,694
[Emilia grunts]

136
00:07:24,777 --> 00:07:28,239
No matter what you do,
no one will hear you.

137
00:07:28,322 --> 00:07:31,993
-[shrieking]
-Remember that, Miss Beautiful.

138
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:35,872
[Emilia groaning]

139
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:37,248
[man 1] Just relax.

140
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:40,585
-[Emilia panting]
-[man 1] You smell so good.

141
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:42,712
[man 1] So good!

142
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:45,214
-[grunts]
-[groans]

143
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:47,925
She stabbed me! She stabbed me!

144
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:56,309
I'm giving you my permission.

145
00:07:57,643 --> 00:07:59,353
Do it, Martel.

146
00:07:59,604 --> 00:08:02,732
[upbeat music playing]

147
00:08:02,815 --> 00:08:03,941
[chuckles lightly]

148
00:08:09,155 --> 00:08:11,574
Cheers, my grandson.

149
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:14,702
Cheers to this huge victory.

150
00:08:14,785 --> 00:08:15,995
I promise you…

151
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:19,540
I will win this fight.

152
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,043
Ivy.

153
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:23,794
Cheers!

154
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:27,590
Congressman, Diego is leading--

155
00:08:27,673 --> 00:08:32,386
I don't give a hoot about what they say.

156
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:35,431
I will win.

157
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:40,186
Arnaldo will win.

158
00:08:42,396 --> 00:08:45,608
The Ardientes always win.

159
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:50,863
Miss Ivy Aguas…

160
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:55,576
I don't care if I have to bomb a truck,

161
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:57,870
a precinct,

162
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:01,958
or even a whole building.

163
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:08,422
I will do all that to ensure my victory.

164
00:09:08,506 --> 00:09:10,049
Remember that.

165
00:09:15,096 --> 00:09:20,184
Whatever it takes
to keep my grandson happy.

166
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:24,772
And to keep this family name on top.

167
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:34,156
My grandson…

168
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,748
Victory is yours.

169
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:51,924
[dramatic music playing]

170
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:17,158
Arnaldo?

171
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:26,959
<i>Yes! I am! I am Lily Cruz!</i>

172
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:29,503
<i>I am Lily Cruz! I am!</i>

173
00:10:34,717 --> 00:10:35,801
Arnaldo.

174
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:39,055
Arnaldo, my grandson.

175
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:44,852
Arnaldo.

176
00:10:48,230 --> 00:10:49,357
Arnaldo?

177
00:10:50,608 --> 00:10:55,613
[dramatic music playing]

178
00:11:01,994 --> 00:11:04,997
[wheezing]

179
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:09,919
[Julio] Yes? Yes?

180
00:11:10,002 --> 00:11:11,754
What is it? What is it?!

181
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:14,173
-[groaning]
-Tell me!

182
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:16,008
[groaning]

183
00:11:16,509 --> 00:11:18,469
-Arnaldo?
-[groaning]

184
00:11:19,095 --> 00:11:21,347
Friends! Here it is!

185
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:23,057
The partial unofficial tally.

186
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:27,770
Diego got 725,364 votes!

187
00:11:27,853 --> 00:11:32,066
-[cheering]
-Okay, okay. Wait, wait, wait.

188
00:11:32,149 --> 00:11:34,193
Guess how many votes Ardiente got.

189
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:37,321
-What?
-He only got 421,000 votes!

190
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:39,281
[cheering]

191
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:42,576
Friends! We only have
one neighborhood left.

192
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:45,371
You basically won, Batch!

193
00:11:45,454 --> 00:11:48,457
[cheering]

194
00:11:48,541 --> 00:11:49,667
-Go, Diego!
-Batch.

195
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:53,671
One neighborhood left!
You've surely won this!

196
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:56,215
-Batch. It's a win.
-We won.

197
00:11:56,298 --> 00:11:57,550
-Diego…
-The new governor!

198
00:11:57,633 --> 00:12:00,636
We succeeded. You succeeded.

199
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:04,140
-[cheering]
-Auntie… Auntie…

200
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:05,474
[Pandoy] Yes! Yes!

201
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:07,143
Auntie, this is everyone's victory.

202
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:09,520
Long live Governor Diego Torillo!

203
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:12,273
-Governor Diego!
-Governor Diego!

204
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:17,361
[cheering]

205
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:19,238
[man] Long live!

206
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:23,451
-[cheering continues]
-[man] To Diego!

207
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:25,411
Uh…

208
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:27,705
[Arnaldo groaning]

209
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:28,873
-Arnaldo.
-Nurse!

210
00:12:28,956 --> 00:12:31,792
Arnaldo, what's wrong?
Tell me so I can help you.

211
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:34,628
-Tell me! Tell me! Tell me!
-Nurse! Nurse!

212
00:12:35,337 --> 00:12:37,548
Tell me. What is it? I… I can help you.

213
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:43,721
[groaning continues]

214
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,184
[nurse] Relax, sir.

215
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:52,271
[cheering]

216
00:12:52,354 --> 00:12:53,355
[Camia] Cheers!

217
00:12:53,439 --> 00:12:54,773
-[cheering]
-[indistinct chatter]

218
00:12:54,857 --> 00:12:56,358
[line rings]

219
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:58,611
[phone rings]

220
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:01,906
-[tense music playing]
-[ringing continues]

221
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:03,324
[line ringing]

222
00:13:09,455 --> 00:13:12,500
-One more. Just a bit more.
-One more town.

223
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:17,588
[screams]

224
00:13:17,671 --> 00:13:19,423
[shrieks]

225
00:13:19,507 --> 00:13:21,717
-[man] Hey, what happened?
-[indistinct chatter]

226
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,385
-Why'd it stop working?
-I don't know.

227
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:25,012
Calm down, guys. It's all right.

228
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:27,139
Listen, everyone! Wait! Wait!

229
00:13:27,223 --> 00:13:28,557
Everyone!

230
00:13:28,641 --> 00:13:31,185
Citizens of Ardiente, let's not panic.

231
00:13:31,268 --> 00:13:32,728
Please, stay calm. And no pushing.

232
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:34,480
Let's not get anyone hurt.

233
00:13:34,563 --> 00:13:36,607
Let's make this a peaceful election.

234
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:40,694
Diego, 90% of Poblacion Ardiente
has just lost electricity.

235
00:13:40,778 --> 00:13:41,820
-Oh, no.
-No…

236
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:44,823
I bet this is part
of Julio Ardiente's plan

237
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:47,451
to sabotage the election once again.

238
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,620
What are we going to do, Diego?

239
00:13:49,703 --> 00:13:52,540
How can we stop Julio
from sabotaging the election?

240
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:54,416
-[Camia] Geez!
-We don't have control

241
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,377
over the system's data.

242
00:13:56,460 --> 00:14:00,839
But we can ask for
additional poll watchers.

243
00:14:00,923 --> 00:14:04,343
Tell them to make sure the votes
won't be tampered with.

244
00:14:04,843 --> 00:14:05,970
Mister Danny, Mister Jun,

245
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:09,056
please tell our poll watchers
to be on their guard.

246
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:11,850
-Hurry! Now!
-Come on! Hurry!

247
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:13,310
Take care.

248
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:18,399
[Arnaldo groaning]

249
00:14:19,316 --> 00:14:20,568
Hon, what's happening?

250
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:22,236
[groaning]

251
00:14:22,570 --> 00:14:23,571
Honey.

252
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,282
Give him some sedatives.

253
00:14:26,365 --> 00:14:28,909
It's okay, hon.
It's okay, Arnaldo. I'm here.

254
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,369
[cries]

255
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:33,831
-Your grandpa is here.
-[groans]

256
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:36,500
-Hon.
-Arnaldo. Arnaldo!

257
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:39,295
I'm here. I'm here.

258
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:44,717
[Arnaldo crying]

259
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:46,468
Excuse me. Let me handle this.

260
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,178
Hon, it's okay.

261
00:14:48,762 --> 00:14:49,930
I'm here, hon.

262
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:56,478
Nurse, what… what happened? Is he okay?

263
00:14:56,562 --> 00:15:01,567
[tense music playing]

264
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,752
Sorry, I can't get any updates
because of the power outage.

265
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:22,796
When can they restore the power supply?

266
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,715
They don't know yet.

267
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:27,134
But no matter how long this takes,

268
00:15:27,217 --> 00:15:29,845
I'm sure you'll still win, Diego.

269
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:33,432
You already had a huge lead
even before the power went out.

270
00:15:34,224 --> 00:15:36,644
Besides, the remaining votes
are from Diego's bailiwick.

271
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:39,730
-There's no way Julio will win.
-[Pandoy] Remember, dear.

272
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:44,193
We're facing Julio Ardiente.
Anything can still happen.

273
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:48,155
-Don't be such a pessimist.
-I'm just stating facts.

274
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:52,034
As long as no one cheats,
it'll be Diego's win for sure.

275
00:15:52,117 --> 00:15:54,954
I've lived here all my life, remember?

276
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:57,957
I know what that Julio is capable of.

277
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,292
Uncle, calm down. Please.

278
00:16:00,376 --> 00:16:05,172
[tense music playing]

279
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:15,808
[Emilia panting]

280
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:27,903
-[shrieks]
-<i>Jaguar ordered us to get you.</i>

281
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:29,405
[gunshots]

282
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:42,876
Oh!

283
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,461
-The power's back!
-They're working again.

284
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:48,966
-Batch, please ask for updates.
-Okay. I'll be right back.

285
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:51,218
-All right, he's on his way.
-Thank goodness.

286
00:16:56,265 --> 00:17:00,728
Doc, can you please explain
what's happening to Arnaldo?

287
00:17:00,811 --> 00:17:03,313
Sometimes, this happens to patients

288
00:17:03,397 --> 00:17:05,649
who've woken up from a coma.

289
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:08,318
-[doctor] So, we don't…
-[Jose] Congressman.

290
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:09,361
[voices drop out]

291
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:11,196
Sir, there's an update on the votes.

292
00:17:12,072 --> 00:17:15,743
-[tense music playing]
-[no audible dialogue]

293
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:22,875
-[tense music playing]
-[no audible dialogue]

294
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:24,501
[Julio] Your news…

295
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:29,339
just made my day.

296
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:30,507
[no audible dialogue]

297
00:17:30,883 --> 00:17:34,094
-Batch. Batch.
-This is something else.

298
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:37,681
-The results just came out.
-How was it?

299
00:17:39,683 --> 00:17:41,018
Batch, come on.

300
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:43,437
What happened? Did Diego win?

301
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:47,399
-Batch?
-Julio Ardiente's winning.

302
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:48,859
-Huh?
-What?

303
00:17:50,652 --> 00:17:51,945
That can't be true.

304
00:17:53,405 --> 00:17:55,032
-Julio cheated!
-[Julio's supporters cheer]

305
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:57,785
-You cheaters!
-Auntie Camia.

306
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:00,287
-You sabotaged the election!
-[Julio's supporters cheer]

307
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:03,624
-Cheaters!
-[Pandoy] This isn't over!

308
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,044
We know what the truth is!

309
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:09,046
[unintelligible]

310
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:10,672
[man] This isn't over!

311
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,008
Don't rejoice just yet!

312
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:15,094
[unintelligible]

313
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:19,431
[Jose] Congressman. Everybody!

314
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:26,105
We are leading by 151,560 votes
over Diego Torillo.

315
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:29,983
That means we've won. Viva Ardiente!

316
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:32,945
[cheering]

317
00:18:33,028 --> 00:18:35,948
[dramatic music playing]

318
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:38,617
Raise your voices, everyone.

319
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:44,540
Shout louder until we can
all be heard by our enemies.

320
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:50,129
So they'll know that we remain the rulers

321
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:53,340
of Poblacion Ardiente. Viva Ardiente!

322
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:55,592
[all] Viva Ardiente!

323
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:59,680
[cheering]

324
00:18:59,763 --> 00:19:03,517
[dramatic music playing]

325
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,811
Thank you. Thank you.

326
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:08,689
Hey, who won for president?

327
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:10,440
My candidate! Who else?

328
00:19:11,108 --> 00:19:13,986
[man 1] Yeah, right. What did
he ever do for the country?

329
00:19:14,069 --> 00:19:16,029
He's all talk, no action.

330
00:19:16,655 --> 00:19:20,492
That's our country for you.
We never learn.

331
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:24,454
<i>We bring you the latest partial</i>
<i>and unofficial vote count</i>

332
00:19:24,538 --> 00:19:29,293
<i>covering 99% of polling precincts</i>
<i>for the gubernatorial election</i>

333
00:19:29,376 --> 00:19:31,128
<i>in the province of Ardiente.</i>

334
00:19:32,087 --> 00:19:34,006
<i>The competition</i>
<i>in this province is fierce.</i>

335
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:39,178
<i>952,896 votes have been counted</i>
<i>for Julio Ardiente,</i>

336
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:44,474
<i>while 801,336 votes have been</i>
<i>counted for Diego Torillo.</i>

337
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:48,896
<i>The people have spoken!</i>
<i>We now have a new governor.</i>

338
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:51,565
<i>The pillar of the entire</i>
<i>province of Ardiente,</i>

339
00:19:51,648 --> 00:19:54,484
<i>the father of the people, Julio Ardiente!</i>

340
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:55,527
[supporters] <i>Long live!</i>

341
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:58,989
<i>-Viva Ardiente!</i>
<i>-Viva Ardiente!</i>

342
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:04,077
[unsettling music playing]

343
00:20:08,415 --> 00:20:11,126
You lying, cheating, old man.

344
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:13,545
You abandoned me.

345
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:18,175
I hate you. You should've just let me die.

346
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:28,352
I'd like to extend
my gratitude to you all.

347
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:34,399
Thank you for trusting me,
for voting for me,

348
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:36,944
and for helping me land this victory.

349
00:20:37,986 --> 00:20:40,030
Again, please accept my deepest thanks.

350
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:42,699
And, as early as now,

351
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:49,039
I'm telling you, I cannot
govern this land alone.

352
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:54,711
And that's why, this early on,
I'm calling on each

353
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:59,132
and every one of you
to help me with my term

354
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:03,220
so that we can restore the former beauty

355
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:07,975
and splendor of Poblacion Ardiente.

356
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:11,603
Let us take our land
back from our enemies!

357
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:15,732
[cheering]

358
00:21:19,778 --> 00:21:22,698
I'd also like to dedicate this victory…

359
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:28,120
to my one and only grandson, Arnaldo!

360
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:33,166
Arnaldo, who, truthfully,

361
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:36,211
should be the one standing here right now.

362
00:21:36,295 --> 00:21:39,923
The one standing here
in my place as governor,

363
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:42,301
as governor of the people.

364
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:49,933
He'd be here if not for
those hooligans he fell victim to.

365
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:52,811
He's now in critical condition.

366
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:56,606
Remember this.

367
00:21:58,066 --> 00:22:03,613
We're going to take back
our town from the hands of those

368
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:08,327
who plan to take it for themselves.

369
00:22:09,494 --> 00:22:16,043
And my new slogan is:
To a new Ardiente for Arnaldo!

370
00:22:16,126 --> 00:22:20,797
For Arnaldo! For Arnaldo!

371
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:22,674
Viva Ardiente!

372
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:26,053
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

373
00:22:26,136 --> 00:22:28,513
Viva Ardiente!

374
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:32,684
[cheering]

375
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:49,117
Arnaldo.

376
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,912
Arnaldo, my son.

377
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:55,665
We've finally won the election.

378
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:59,336
Isn't this what I promised you?

379
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:03,465
That I'd make this family rise once more?

380
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:11,056
And I am going to roll out
the red carpet for when you return.

381
00:23:14,017 --> 00:23:16,978
But you have to help me.

382
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:24,319
Arnaldo, tell me who did this to you.

383
00:23:25,987 --> 00:23:30,450
Tell me who should pay.

384
00:23:38,583 --> 00:23:39,668
Arnaldo.

385
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:42,629
Arnaldo, talk to me.

386
00:23:52,347 --> 00:23:55,350
Tell me who should pay.

387
00:23:57,978 --> 00:24:02,983
[tense music playing]

388
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:07,946
[cocks gun]

389
00:24:16,204 --> 00:24:17,539
Arnaldo.

390
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:19,291
Talk to me.

391
00:24:19,749 --> 00:24:20,917
Speak.

392
00:24:22,169 --> 00:24:23,211
Please.

393
00:24:23,587 --> 00:24:24,671
Talk to me.

394
00:24:29,426 --> 00:24:31,928
-[groaning]
-[beeping accelerating]

395
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:33,930
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

396
00:24:34,014 --> 00:24:35,849
Nurse! Nurse!

397
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:37,350
Arnaldo! Arnaldo!

398
00:24:37,434 --> 00:24:39,769
-[Ivy] Nurse!
-Arnaldo! Nurse!

399
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:41,271
[nurse] Excuse me, please.

400
00:24:48,445 --> 00:24:50,071
Please do something, doc.

401
00:24:50,155 --> 00:24:53,283
-Take note of the seizure.
-What's going on, doc?!

402
00:24:53,366 --> 00:24:56,203
Nurse, administer relaxant, 10 cc.

403
00:24:56,494 --> 00:25:01,458
[unsettling music playing]

404
00:25:04,836 --> 00:25:05,962
Hon.

405
00:25:08,715 --> 00:25:10,091
What's happening?

406
00:25:34,783 --> 00:25:37,494
[doctor] It is hard to see
Mayor Ardiente suffer,

407
00:25:37,577 --> 00:25:39,454
but I have to be honest with you.

408
00:25:39,955 --> 00:25:43,333
He may continue to experience
episodes of seizures

409
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:46,670
due to the abnormal electrical
activity of his brain,

410
00:25:46,753 --> 00:25:49,923
and he may remain in a catatonic state.

411
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:53,760
It's possible that when
he regains consciousness,

412
00:25:53,843 --> 00:25:57,180
he may not remember anything
about what happened to him

413
00:25:57,264 --> 00:25:58,556
before he got shot,

414
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:00,934
and this is due to temporary amnesia.

415
00:26:03,687 --> 00:26:06,731
Doc, how long will he stay like this?

416
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:08,316
It's hard to say.

417
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:10,944
It might take him months
before he can fully recover

418
00:26:11,027 --> 00:26:14,489
and regain all his memory back.
Please rest assured that

419
00:26:14,572 --> 00:26:17,409
we're doing everything we can
to help him recover immediately.

420
00:26:18,159 --> 00:26:19,744
Please, doc. Please.

421
00:26:21,621 --> 00:26:23,790
-Thank you.
-Excuse me.

422
00:26:27,043 --> 00:26:29,296
[Ivy] At least, Congressman…

423
00:26:30,046 --> 00:26:33,049
At least Arnaldo's awake now.
That's a good sign.

424
00:26:34,759 --> 00:26:37,387
And I have you to thank for that.

425
00:26:38,430 --> 00:26:44,769
I know your visits have
helped his recovery a lot.

426
00:26:45,854 --> 00:26:47,939
-And…
-[exhales deeply]

427
00:26:48,023 --> 00:26:51,192
As soon Arnaldo is fully recovered…

428
00:26:52,235 --> 00:26:54,988
I still want you two to get married.

429
00:26:56,656 --> 00:26:57,699
Thank you.

430
00:26:58,116 --> 00:27:03,330
It's nice to hear that we both
want the same thing to happen.

431
00:27:05,623 --> 00:27:09,169
I don't want you to be
separated from us, Ivy.

432
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:11,421
You know…

433
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:17,802
You and I, we make
beautiful music together.

434
00:27:19,387 --> 00:27:21,514
My winning the election proves

435
00:27:21,598 --> 00:27:25,810
that we are the team to contend with.

436
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:30,065
Because maybe I'm your lucky charm.

437
00:27:30,148 --> 00:27:31,316
Nah.

438
00:27:32,859 --> 00:27:34,861
You're not my lucky charm.

439
00:27:36,196 --> 00:27:39,783
You're the daughter that I never had.

440
00:27:44,913 --> 00:27:45,872
[Ivy exhales deeply]

441
00:27:45,955 --> 00:27:48,792
I'm happy to be part
of your family, Cong--

442
00:27:49,793 --> 00:27:51,628
I'm sorry, you're not
a congressman anymore.

443
00:27:51,711 --> 00:27:53,588
[chuckles]

444
00:27:53,671 --> 00:27:57,175
Governor. Governor Julio Ardiente.

445
00:27:58,468 --> 00:28:02,389
Congratulations. Your new title suits you.

446
00:28:02,931 --> 00:28:04,933
Congratulations, Governor.

447
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:09,938
I must admit. It has a certain ring to it.

448
00:28:11,189 --> 00:28:17,070
Anyway, my enemies should
start saying their prayers.

449
00:28:18,238 --> 00:28:21,074
Because this is
the beginning of their end.

450
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:24,869
And I want you to be by my side…

451
00:28:26,121 --> 00:28:28,248
to watch their demise.

452
00:28:32,001 --> 00:28:34,796
Just send the invitation,
and I'll be there.

453
00:28:41,010 --> 00:28:46,015
[ominous music playing]

454
00:28:50,228 --> 00:28:52,689
You can count on it, woman.

455
00:28:53,690 --> 00:28:55,150
You can count on it.

456
00:29:01,948 --> 00:29:03,533
Gentlemen, listen up.

457
00:29:04,367 --> 00:29:09,038
Just because we won the election
doesn't mean the fight is over.

458
00:29:09,122 --> 00:29:14,627
Believe me,
Diego's little group won't stop.

459
00:29:14,711 --> 00:29:18,923
They will all go through
the post-election motions,

460
00:29:19,007 --> 00:29:23,178
starting off with a protest.
But I've got news for them.

461
00:29:23,970 --> 00:29:28,933
I am also declaring war
against the opposition.

462
00:29:30,393 --> 00:29:33,354
Hear me. I don't care how you do it.

463
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:41,654
Practice zero tolerance whether
it be your wife, your children,

464
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:47,076
your mother, your mother-in-law,
or your servants in the house.

465
00:29:47,786 --> 00:29:52,791
Do whatever is necessary. Use every means.

466
00:29:53,166 --> 00:29:56,002
But I want to put a stop
to the opposition.

467
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:58,963
I want all this to end.

468
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:00,340
Remember this…

469
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:05,136
the enemies and opponents
of Julio Ardiente…

470
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:10,767
are the enemies and opponents
of the people of Ardiente.

471
00:30:19,692 --> 00:30:23,446
I can't let Julio Ardiente take office.

472
00:30:24,864 --> 00:30:27,033
We can't. We have to stop his cheating.

473
00:30:27,116 --> 00:30:28,493
His lying to the people.

474
00:30:28,993 --> 00:30:30,537
We can't let this keep happening.

475
00:30:30,954 --> 00:30:32,121
You're right, Lily.

476
00:30:32,205 --> 00:30:34,415
That Julio Ardiente has some nerve.

477
00:30:34,499 --> 00:30:36,626
Diego should be the one taking office.

478
00:30:37,085 --> 00:30:40,922
Dear, we need to oust him
before Arnaldo gets better

479
00:30:41,005 --> 00:30:43,967
and before Julio finds out
that you're Lily.

480
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:47,303
We'll prove his cheating.

481
00:30:48,096 --> 00:30:49,764
We have a lot of potential evidence.

482
00:30:52,183 --> 00:30:53,893
You're right.
We do have a lot of evidence.

483
00:30:54,477 --> 00:30:55,687
Thank you, Diego.

484
00:30:57,230 --> 00:31:00,275
As long as we don't give up,

485
00:31:00,358 --> 00:31:01,985
there is hope.

486
00:31:02,485 --> 00:31:06,865
I will never accept defeat,
so we will keep fighting.

487
00:31:07,448 --> 00:31:08,950
You will win, Diego.

488
00:31:09,242 --> 00:31:14,247
[dramatic music playing]

489
00:31:29,262 --> 00:31:30,722
-[clapping]
-[woman] People of Ardiente!

490
00:31:30,805 --> 00:31:36,311
Here is Poblacion Ardiente's new
governor, Mr. Julio Ardiente.

491
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:39,731
[cheering]

492
00:31:39,814 --> 00:31:42,942
[chanting] Ardiente! Ardiente!

493
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:49,741
[chanting] Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

494
00:31:49,824 --> 00:31:55,538
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente!

495
00:31:55,622 --> 00:31:58,458
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

496
00:31:58,541 --> 00:32:00,126
[man shouting] Governor Julio!

497
00:32:00,209 --> 00:32:02,629
[chanting continues]

498
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:08,259
[cheering]

499
00:32:09,344 --> 00:32:14,057
[supporters whooping and chanting]

500
00:32:14,891 --> 00:32:16,476
[man] We love you!

501
00:32:16,559 --> 00:32:19,771
[cheering continues]

502
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:22,440
[man] We love you, Governor Julio!

503
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:29,948
[chanting] Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

504
00:32:30,323 --> 00:32:33,701
-Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

505
00:32:34,243 --> 00:32:36,454
Thank you very much.
Please take your seats!

506
00:32:38,331 --> 00:32:42,961
Once again, I would like
to thank all the residents

507
00:32:43,044 --> 00:32:44,837
of the province of Ardiente
who voted for me.

508
00:32:44,921 --> 00:32:49,175
Thank you for giving me
another opportunity

509
00:32:49,258 --> 00:32:53,763
to serve you as your governor.

510
00:32:54,472 --> 00:32:55,932
I promise you…

511
00:32:56,891 --> 00:32:59,811
that I will restore peace
and order in our province.

512
00:32:59,894 --> 00:33:02,814
[cheering]

513
00:33:05,483 --> 00:33:08,736
And I will not bow down

514
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:15,827
to anyone who ever tries
to hinder the progress

515
00:33:15,910 --> 00:33:18,579
that I dream for the province of Ardiente.

516
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:22,041
And remember this…

517
00:33:22,750 --> 00:33:27,839
While your Governor Julio
is here to lead you…

518
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:36,764
there will be no place
for rebels here in our home.

519
00:33:37,181 --> 00:33:40,393
[crowd clapping]

520
00:33:40,476 --> 00:33:45,023
[chanting] Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

521
00:33:45,106 --> 00:33:47,650
-Comrades, wait! Wait!
-[car beeping]

522
00:33:47,734 --> 00:33:53,031
[frantic screaming]

523
00:33:53,114 --> 00:33:55,408
You monster! Are you trying to kill us?!

524
00:33:56,826 --> 00:33:58,578
-Curse those Ardientes!
-Hey!

525
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:00,079
Are you okay?

526
00:34:00,371 --> 00:34:04,083
Those damn Ardientes! Shame on you!

527
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:06,627
-Don't move. Don't move.
-Curse those Ardientes!

528
00:34:06,711 --> 00:34:07,962
Hey, let's help him!

529
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:10,631
-Pandoy!
-Someone call for help! Hurry!

530
00:34:10,715 --> 00:34:11,674
Hang on.

531
00:34:11,758 --> 00:34:14,719
Danny, this is very valuable.

532
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:17,013
Diego can use this against the Ardientes.

533
00:34:17,096 --> 00:34:18,514
-I understand.
-So, tomorrow…

534
00:34:18,598 --> 00:34:20,308
deliver this to the headquarters.

535
00:34:20,391 --> 00:34:22,060
-Okay.
-[thud]

536
00:34:22,143 --> 00:34:23,311
What's this?

537
00:34:24,729 --> 00:34:25,980
Men, search the house!

538
00:34:28,107 --> 00:34:30,193
-[groans]
-Search the whole house!

539
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:32,779
You're Ardiente's men, aren't you?

540
00:34:34,155 --> 00:34:35,281
[Fernan] What are you--

541
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:38,618
-Give that back!
-Take those!

542
00:34:38,701 --> 00:34:41,871
-Hey.
-[groans]

543
00:34:44,123 --> 00:34:46,751
[Divine] Your new clothes look great!

544
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:48,336
[man] Divine Uytengco.

545
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:50,463
-[gunshot]
-[screaming]

546
00:34:53,841 --> 00:34:57,303
Help! Help!

547
00:34:57,386 --> 00:35:01,516
Mommy! Mom, no! No! No, please!

548
00:35:01,599 --> 00:35:05,144
Mommy! No! Mommy!

549
00:35:05,228 --> 00:35:08,731
Help, please! Help!

550
00:35:08,815 --> 00:35:13,945
[dramatic music playing]

551
00:35:15,613 --> 00:35:18,241
-[gunshots]
-[screaming]

552
00:35:18,324 --> 00:35:19,659
No!

553
00:35:20,201 --> 00:35:21,702
-[gunshot]
-[groans]

554
00:35:29,585 --> 00:35:32,839
-Viva Ardiente!
-Viva Ardiente!

555
00:35:32,922 --> 00:35:38,219
[chanting] Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

556
00:35:38,302 --> 00:35:43,891
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente!

557
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:49,438
Viva Ardiente!
Viva Ardiente! Viva Ardiente!

558
00:35:49,522 --> 00:35:51,232
Viva Ardiente!

559
00:35:51,315 --> 00:35:57,655
[chanting] Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

560
00:35:58,656 --> 00:36:00,741
Mr. Diego Torillo, why are you here?

561
00:36:00,825 --> 00:36:02,618
We are here to protest against

562
00:36:02,702 --> 00:36:07,540
Julio Ardiente's proclamation
as governor of this province.

563
00:36:07,790 --> 00:36:10,084
Because aside from harassment
and vote-buying,

564
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:12,712
cheating also took place
in the last election.

565
00:36:12,795 --> 00:36:15,464
Before the power blackout,
our party was leading.

566
00:36:15,548 --> 00:36:17,717
But they took the lead
when electricity was restored!

567
00:36:17,800 --> 00:36:21,554
What is this?! We are not dumb!
According to our investigation,

568
00:36:21,637 --> 00:36:23,264
the data that was
transferred to the server

569
00:36:23,347 --> 00:36:25,349
did not come from the voting precincts.

570
00:36:25,433 --> 00:36:28,728
It came from an unidentified source.

571
00:36:28,811 --> 00:36:32,732
That's why we're certain that
the Ardientes cheated us.

572
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:35,526
-Right, everyone?
-That's right!

573
00:36:35,610 --> 00:36:38,237
Mr. Diego, how will you
prove these allegations?

574
00:36:38,321 --> 00:36:39,780
We'll request a preserve order

575
00:36:39,864 --> 00:36:42,742
to determine the real number of voters.

576
00:36:42,825 --> 00:36:45,995
So, Julio Ardiente, I am challenging you.

577
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:51,000
If you truly didn't cheat, I am
challenging you to a recount

578
00:36:51,083 --> 00:36:56,047
to find out who the people
of this province voted for!

579
00:36:56,130 --> 00:36:57,715
That's right!

580
00:36:57,798 --> 00:37:01,093
[chanting] Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

581
00:37:01,177 --> 00:37:07,475
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

582
00:37:07,558 --> 00:37:10,645
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

583
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:16,776
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

584
00:37:16,859 --> 00:37:20,238
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

585
00:37:20,321 --> 00:37:26,702
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

586
00:37:26,786 --> 00:37:29,830
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

587
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:36,379
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

588
00:37:36,462 --> 00:37:38,172
[chanting continues]

589
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:42,468
What do you think I ought to do to people

590
00:37:42,551 --> 00:37:45,263
starting riots in my province?

591
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:50,184
Governor, they're just fighting
for what they think is right.

592
00:37:50,268 --> 00:37:53,729
And I don't see anything wrong with it.

593
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:57,441
They're like us. They stand
for what they believe in.

594
00:37:58,150 --> 00:38:03,155
I am nothing like those scum.

595
00:38:03,656 --> 00:38:08,452
They are like rats who try
to steal someone else's food.

596
00:38:09,245 --> 00:38:13,791
Do you know what we do
to pests in this province?

597
00:38:13,874 --> 00:38:15,293
[protesters continue chanting]

598
00:38:15,376 --> 00:38:21,090
We annihilate them
before they can become a plague

599
00:38:21,173 --> 00:38:24,927
and run the town into the ground.

600
00:38:25,011 --> 00:38:27,513
[protesters continue chanting]

601
00:38:27,596 --> 00:38:31,726
Sanggano. You know what to do.

602
00:38:31,809 --> 00:38:32,727
Yes, Governor.

603
00:38:32,810 --> 00:38:37,398
-[protesters continue chanting]
-[tense music playing]

604
00:38:37,481 --> 00:38:42,069
Miss Aguas, relax and enjoy the show.

605
00:38:42,153 --> 00:38:43,988
[protesters continue chanting]

606
00:38:44,071 --> 00:38:47,491
[chanting] Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

607
00:38:47,575 --> 00:38:49,535
[chanting continues]

608
00:38:49,618 --> 00:38:52,330
Auntie! Anna! Hide in the back.
Batch, go with them.

609
00:38:52,413 --> 00:38:53,331
Come on.

610
00:38:53,414 --> 00:38:59,128
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!
Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

611
00:38:59,211 --> 00:39:00,463
Stand together!

612
00:39:00,546 --> 00:39:03,382
-[protesters continue chanting]
-[tense music playing]

613
00:39:03,466 --> 00:39:04,467
Hold on!

614
00:39:07,470 --> 00:39:11,515
Friends! Don't let go! Don't let go!

615
00:39:12,767 --> 00:39:17,355
[chanting] Julio Ardiente is a cheater!

616
00:39:17,438 --> 00:39:22,485
-[protesters continue chanting]
-[clamoring]

617
00:39:22,568 --> 00:39:26,197
[protesters continue chanting]

618
00:39:26,280 --> 00:39:27,573
[Diego] Don't let go!

619
00:39:27,656 --> 00:39:31,118
-[protesters continue chanting]
-[tense music playing]

620
00:39:31,202 --> 00:39:37,583
[protesters chanting, clamoring]

621
00:39:37,666 --> 00:39:41,670
-Hold tight!
-Don't let go!

622
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:44,507
[tense music continues]

623
00:39:44,590 --> 00:39:46,759
[frantic screaming]

624
00:39:46,842 --> 00:39:51,430
[commotion intensifies]

625
00:39:51,514 --> 00:39:54,433
[frantic screaming]

626
00:40:00,689 --> 00:40:02,483
Can you please stop this, Governor?

627
00:40:03,317 --> 00:40:06,487
Miss Aguas, are you not entertained?

628
00:40:08,197 --> 00:40:11,742
[commotion continues]

629
00:40:11,826 --> 00:40:13,035
Forward!

630
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:18,124
[frantic screaming]

631
00:40:22,878 --> 00:40:23,712
[woman screams]

632
00:40:25,756 --> 00:40:26,549
[shrieking]

633
00:40:32,721 --> 00:40:35,599
-Don't let go!
-Hold on!

634
00:40:35,683 --> 00:40:37,643
Hold tight! Hold tight!

635
00:40:37,726 --> 00:40:38,686
Let me go!

636
00:40:38,769 --> 00:40:43,107
[commotion continues over tense music]

637
00:40:43,190 --> 00:40:46,152
Tell your men to stop this, please!

638
00:40:48,320 --> 00:40:50,906
Who are you to give me orders?

639
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:59,707
I am Julio Ardiente,
governor of Poblacion Ardiente.

640
00:40:59,790 --> 00:41:03,377
And no one tells me what to do!

641
00:41:04,628 --> 00:41:06,797
Especially not you.

642
00:41:09,341 --> 00:41:14,346
[frantic screaming]

643
00:41:17,808 --> 00:41:19,810
[commotion continues]

644
00:41:20,936 --> 00:41:25,191
Miss Aguas, why are you so upset?

645
00:41:27,234 --> 00:41:29,528
What kind of question is that?
Who wouldn't be?!

646
00:41:29,612 --> 00:41:31,697
Look what you're doing to them!

647
00:41:31,780 --> 00:41:33,240
You have just been elected governor.

648
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:36,577
You're supposed to work
on winning their support!

649
00:41:36,660 --> 00:41:39,288
Not egging them on!

650
00:41:39,371 --> 00:41:44,335
Your term might end early
if you don't stop this now!

651
00:41:44,418 --> 00:41:49,131
Anna! Auntie Camia! Auntie! Auntie Camia!

652
00:41:49,632 --> 00:41:52,801
[frantic screaming]

653
00:41:52,885 --> 00:41:54,011
[grunts]

654
00:41:54,094 --> 00:41:55,387
[Anna screaming]

655
00:41:56,347 --> 00:41:59,141
[tense music playing]

656
00:41:59,225 --> 00:42:01,477
I have the money.

657
00:42:02,019 --> 00:42:04,563
I am in a position of power.

658
00:42:06,106 --> 00:42:08,859
I have everything I need, Ivy.

659
00:42:09,401 --> 00:42:14,573
I don't need the help of my enemies.

660
00:42:14,657 --> 00:42:19,370
If they want to go against me,
well, they better be prepared

661
00:42:19,453 --> 00:42:22,498
to face the consequences of their actions.

662
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:27,503
Well then, excuse me.
I'm not in the mood for violence.

663
00:42:27,586 --> 00:42:28,921
[Julio] Wait a minute.

664
00:42:33,050 --> 00:42:36,303
Don't tell me you're acting that way

665
00:42:36,387 --> 00:42:39,890
because you feel sorry for those morons?

666
00:42:39,974 --> 00:42:42,393
Do you really want to know why?

667
00:42:42,476 --> 00:42:45,062
[protesters clamoring]

668
00:42:45,145 --> 00:42:47,356
Let me remind you, Governor,

669
00:42:48,023 --> 00:42:51,318
that I invested a huge sum
in your campaign.

670
00:42:51,777 --> 00:42:54,405
But if your term will end early,

671
00:42:54,488 --> 00:42:56,907
how am I supposed to get back
all that I've put in?

672
00:42:56,991 --> 00:43:00,202
Stop treating me like I'm your enemy

673
00:43:00,286 --> 00:43:02,371
because I'm just looking out for you.

674
00:43:02,454 --> 00:43:04,623
And one more thing, Governor.

675
00:43:05,416 --> 00:43:09,712
You need me more than I need you!

676
00:43:09,795 --> 00:43:14,800
[tense music playing]

677
00:43:17,428 --> 00:43:20,055
[protesters clamoring]

678
00:43:24,727 --> 00:43:29,690
[frantic screaming]

679
00:43:29,773 --> 00:43:34,862
[tense music continues playing]

680
00:43:40,534 --> 00:43:42,161
[music fading]

681
00:43:43,120 --> 00:43:48,125
[somber music playing]

682
00:43:59,386 --> 00:44:03,015
<i>This is precisely why</i>
<i>I could not love you!</i>

683
00:44:03,098 --> 00:44:07,645
<i>Because you're no different</i>
<i>from your treacherous mother!</i>

684
00:44:07,728 --> 00:44:10,939
<i>Get out of my house! Get out!</i> [gunshot]

685
00:44:11,023 --> 00:44:13,067
<i>-Papa!</i>
<i>-Get out!</i>

686
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:39,343
<i>An Ardiente is not weak.</i>

687
00:44:39,426 --> 00:44:42,137
<i>An Ardiente never loses.</i>

688
00:44:42,221 --> 00:44:46,058
<i>And I will always be an Ardiente.</i>

689
00:44:46,141 --> 00:44:51,105
[ominous music playing]

690
00:44:53,649 --> 00:44:57,319
<i>I will rise up and destroy you all.</i>

691
00:45:05,285 --> 00:45:06,412
<i>Nonsense!</i>

692
00:45:06,495 --> 00:45:08,539
<i>How was Emilia's case whitewashed?!</i>

693
00:45:08,622 --> 00:45:09,706
<i>They got everything.</i>

694
00:45:09,790 --> 00:45:12,334
<i>Who else could've helped Emilia?!</i>

695
00:45:12,418 --> 00:45:15,170
<i>Surprised? I am so back.</i>

696
00:45:15,254 --> 00:45:17,423
<i>-Emilia.</i>
<i>-Hi, Papa.</i>

697
00:45:17,506 --> 00:45:19,758
<i>I've already disowned</i>
<i>that daughter of mine.</i>

698
00:45:19,842 --> 00:45:24,263
[Ivy] <i>Those two are cut from</i>
<i>the same two-faced cloth.</i>

699
00:45:24,346 --> 00:45:25,347
<i>Stay here.</i>

700
00:45:25,431 --> 00:45:27,933
<i>We're attacking Diego's group tonight.</i>

701
00:45:28,016 --> 00:45:28,892
-[gunshots]
-[screaming]

702
00:45:28,976 --> 00:45:31,437
[Ivy] <i>Diego, Julio's men abducted</i>

703
00:45:31,520 --> 00:45:32,729
<i>Anna and your supporters.</i>

704
00:45:32,813 --> 00:45:34,273
<i>They're going to kill them!</i>

705
00:45:34,356 --> 00:45:37,818
<i>-Help!</i>
<i>-Help us!</i>

706
00:45:37,901 --> 00:45:40,404
[theme music playing]
